    "description": "Try this no-fuss dinner recipe that basically cooks itself! In this video, Nicole shows you how to make a creamy slow cooker beef stew. Unlike other slow cooker beef stews, this dish starts by searing the stew meat in a pan over the stove. Once the meat has browned, add it into the slow cooker with vegetables like onion, carrot, and celery. Using beef stock and deglazed sauce from the pan, allow the stew to cook for four to eight hours. It’s thick, tender, and an easy meal that anyone can make!",
